---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WeatherSection from '../../components/WeatherSection.astro';
import TidesSection from '../../components/TidesSection.astro';
import { place, sourceLinks } from '../../data/place';
import { enAttractionSchema } from '../../data/enGuide';

export const prerender = false;

const jsonLd = [enAttractionSchema(Astro.site ? Astro.site.toString() : undefined)];
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Things to Do at Gokarna Main Beach — Sunset, Temple, Swimming & More"
  description="What to do at Gokarna Main Beach: sunrise/sunset, Mahabaleshwar Temple, Om Beach views, photography, food and sea-safety notes."
  image={place.heroImage}
  imageAlt={`${place.fullNameEn}, ${place.cityEn} — things to do`}
  alternates={[{ lang: 'en', href: '/en/things-to-do/' }, { lang: 'x-default', href: '/en/things-to-do/' }]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="shell py-18 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Things to do</p>
      <h1 class="section-title mt-3">What to do at Gokarna Main Beach</h1>
      <p class="lead mt-5">Main Beach is the town-facing gateway: a long sandy shore, the Arabian Sea sunset, and the pilgrimage life of Gokarna all meet here. Pair it with the temple walk and the southern beach string for a fuller day.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="card p-7">
        <p class="text-xs font-extrabold text-temple-500">Sea &amp; sky</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-extrabold text-ocean-900">Sunrise &amp; sunset</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Early light and the evening sunset are the best times on the sand. Check today’s weather and tide below to pick a comfortable window.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-7">
        <p class="text-xs font-extrabold text-temple-500">Pilgrimage</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-extrabold text-ocean-900">Mahabaleshwar Temple</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">The Shaiva religious centre tied to the Atmalinga legend. Follow local dress, photography and entry rules; some devotees bathe at the beach before darshan.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-7">
        <p class="text-xs font-extrabold text-ocean-700">Scenery</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-extrabold text-ocean-900">Om Beach views</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">The two curved bays that look like “Om” from above are reachable south of Main Beach. A classic Gokarna viewpoint for the coastline shape.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card p-7">
        <p class="text-xs font-extrabold text-ocean-700">Culture</p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-extrabold text-ocean-900">Temples &amp; Koti Tirtha</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Maha Ganapati Temple and the sacred pool Koti Tirtha add depth to the temple-area walk. Keep a respectful distance during rituals.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 rounded-[2rem] bg-ocean-900 p-7 text-white md:p-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Sea safety, every time</h2>
      <div class="mt-5 grid gap-4 text-sm leading-7 text-ocean-50/90 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <p>Karnataka Tourism’s current Gokarna guide flags Main Beach as not ideal for swimming because of strong currents. Treat lifeguard/warning flags as the first instruction.</p>
        <p>Coastal currents like rip currents may be invisible. If in doubt, stay at the shore and enjoy the beach instead of going in.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <WeatherSection lang="en" />
  <TidesSection lang="en" />

  <section class="bg-ocean-50 py-18 md:py-24">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow">Food &amp; photography</p>
        <h2 class="section-title mt-3">Around the beach</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="rounded-[1.6rem] border border-ocean-900/10 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold">Coastal food</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">The town has small eateries and coastal/Karnataka food. This site recommends no specific restaurant; choose busy, hygienic places.</p></article>
        <article class="rounded-[1.6rem] border border-ocean-900/10 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold">Photography</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">Golden hours, the bay and coastal rocks give varied frames. Monsoon greens and cloudy light are good for mood shots.</p></article>
        <article class="rounded-[1.6rem] border border-ocean-900/10 bg-white p-6"><h3 class="text-lg font-extrabold">Slow walk</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600">A beach walk at low crowd times, combined with the temple streets, is the simplest way to feel the town’s rhythm.</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/en/" class="rounded-full bg-ocean-900 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white no-underline hover:bg-ocean-700">Back to guide</a>
        <a href="/en/nearby-beaches/" class="rounded-full border border-ocean-900/15 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-ocean-900 no-underline hover:bg-white">Nearby beaches</a>
        <a href="/en/getting-there/" class="rounded-full border border-ocean-900/15 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-ocean-900 no-underline hover:bg-white">How to get there</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell py-18 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs leading-6 text-slate-400">References: <a class="underline" href={sourceLinks.district} rel="noreferrer">Uttara Kannada district</a> · <a class="underline" href={sourceLinks.stateTourism} rel="noreferrer">Karnataka Tourism</a> · <a class="underline" href={sourceLinks.stateBeachGuide} rel="noreferrer">Karnataka Tourism — beaches</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
